  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Educational Quality and Assessment Programme Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Educational Quality and Assessment Programme (EQAP) is the education division of the Pacific Community (SPC). Australia&apos;s partnership with EQAP supports 15 Pacific Island countries&#x2019; efforts to strengthen their education systems, providing education services for regional and national education stakeholders to supplement systems and capabilities, where necessary. EQAP administers the high-profile Pacific Islands Literacy and Numeracy Assessment (PILNA) and the South Pacific Form Seven Certificate (SPFSC). It supports qualifications recognition and quality assurance for technical vocational education and training in the Pacific. EQAP is also a key implementing partner and monitoring and evaluation lead in advancing regional education policy priorities outlined in the Pacific Regional Education Framework (PacREF).</narrative>
  </description>
